# BUGS

`nodes` says what each member's entry is, not whether it answers.

A write of `file` must hold the whole file, and a push sends it in one message: a file larger than one message (about 32 KiB) can be written locally but not pushed.

A member can push any file that passes the checks, including one without itself or without the node it pushes to; the node takes it, and from then on answers only the members the new file lists.
